  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">POTHOLES PLUS PROJECT</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ongoing efforts within Manitoba and the PHJV at]large, to maintain and improve continental waterfowl populations. Rooted in the implementation of the North American Waterfowl Management Plan (NAWMP) and delivered under the guidance of the PHJV and Manitoba NAWMP Implementation Plans, the project will work to restore and sustain waterfowl populations. Specifically, activities include 16,250 acres of perpetual conservation easements (8,125 wetland and 8,125 upland) and 420 acres of conservation agreements (360 wetland and 60 upland). Conservation actions will also enhance 300 wetland acres, manage 77,469 acres (35,763 wetland and 41,706 upland), and stewardship activities will benefit 1,520 acres (760 wetland and 760 upland).</narrative>
  </description>
